{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39836542",
      "title": "Handling Project Deletion",
      "sourceHash": "ca1f297232c59844e09e8cdb68e1bfd39582e26f6a5f6a2fc05585b6d4df0fbf",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.75,
          "end": 4.14,
          "en": "So to make this delete button here work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.14,
          "end": 6.57,
          "en": "we, of course, need to do basically the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.57,
          "end": 8.853,
          "en": "we did a couple of times before already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 12.69,
          "en": "We need to add a function to the app component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.69,
          "end": 17.28,
          "en": "a function which edits this state and removes a project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.28,
          "end": 19.416,
          "en": "And we need to pass that function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.416,
          "end": 23.523,
          "en": "to that selected project component in this case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.9,
          "end": 26.64,
          "en": "So let's do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.64,
          "end": 30.51,
          "en": "For that, I'll add a new function here in the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.51,
          "end": 33.55,
          "en": "a handleDeleteProject function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.41,
          "end": 37.62,
          "en": "and in there, we wanna update the state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.62,
          "end": 42.03,
          "en": "So I'll copy one of those state update function calls here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.03,
          "end": 45.123,
          "en": "and paste it into this handleDeleteProject function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.65,
          "end": 50.34,
          "en": "And now here for one, the selectedProjectID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.34,
          "end": 53.02,
          "en": "should indeed be set back to undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.97,
          "end": 57.48,
          "en": "so that we no longer select that project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.48,
          "end": 60.91,
          "en": "But in addition, the project's array must be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 62.19,
          "end": 65.01,
          "en": "and it should be updated in an immutable way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.01,
          "end": 69.003,
          "en": "so that we don't edit the original array in memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.87,
          "end": 72.45,
          "en": "Now an elegant way of doing that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.45,
          "end": 74.43,
          "en": "is to use the previous state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.43,
          "end": 76.68,
          "en": "and the projects that are stored there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.68,
          "end": 81.68,
          "en": "and calling the filter method, which just like map and find,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.9,
          "end": 84.60300000000001,
          "en": "is a method built into vanilla JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 85.56,
          "end": 90.3,
          "en": "And filter works such that it takes a function as an input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.3,
          "end": 95.22,
          "en": "just like map and find and this function will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 95.22,
          "end": 97.38,
          "en": "for every item in this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 97.38,
          "end": 100.743,
          "en": "Again, just as it's the case for find and map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 101.78999999999999,
          "end": 105.12,
          "en": "But this function should then return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 105.12,
          "end": 107.61,
          "en": "if an element should be kept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.61,
          "end": 110.163,
          "en": "or false if it should be dropped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 115.08,
          "en": "And the filter method will then return a brand new array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.08,
          "end": 118.59,
          "en": "that only contains the elements that were not dropped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 118.59,
          "end": 121.173,
          "en": "So, for which this function yielded true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 122.13,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "Now this function, just like find and map",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 128.04,
          "en": "will receive every item here as a input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 128.04,
          "end": 130.26,
          "en": "And then here we should return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.26,
          "end": 134.013,
          "en": "if we want to keep the item and false if we want to drop it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.39,
          "end": 137.67000000000002,
          "en": "Therefore, here I want to drop the item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 137.67000000000002,
          "end": 141.6,
          "en": "and I wanna return false if the idea of the project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 141.6,
          "end": 145.89,
          "en": "I'm looking at is not equal to the ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 145.89,
          "end": 147.72,
          "en": "that was previously selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 147.72,
          "end": 150.963,
          "en": "because it's this selected item that we're deleting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.97,
          "end": 156.69,
          "en": "So, we can use the previous state and then there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 156.69,
          "end": 157.653,
          "en": "selectedProjectID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 160.088,
          "end": 165.088,
          "en": "If the IDs here do not match, I know that I'm not looking at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 165.45,
          "end": 167.22,
          "en": "the item that should be deleted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 167.22,
          "end": 170.34300000000002,
          "en": "and therefore I'll return true to keep that item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 171.93,
          "end": 175.47,
          "en": "If these IDs do match, I'm looking at the item that should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 175.47,
          "end": 178.98,
          "en": "be deleted and therefore thanks to this comparison here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 178.98,
          "end": 182.103,
          "en": "I'm returning false and the item will be dropped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183.15,
          "end": 186.54,
          "en": "That's how this handleDeleteProject function here will work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 186.54,
          "end": 189.45,
          "en": "and it doesn't even need the ID of the item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.45,
          "end": 192.63,
          "en": "that should be deleted as input because we can get that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 192.63,
          "end": 194.253,
          "en": "from our previous state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 196.23,
          "end": 200.01,
          "en": "So, therefore, now we should pass a pointer to this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 200.01,
          "end": 202.44,
          "en": "to the selected project component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 202.44,
          "end": 206.427,
          "en": "maybe through a prop named \"onDelete\" like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 210.57,
          "end": 213.99,
          "en": "so that we can call this function through that prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 213.99,
          "end": 215.613,
          "en": "from inside that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 217.14,
          "end": 220.71,
          "en": "So, in SelectedProject, we again should extract",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 220.71,
          "end": 225.6,
          "en": "this newly added onDelete prop and then connect it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 225.6,
          "end": 226.863,
          "en": "to this delete button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 227.91,
          "end": 231.18,
          "en": "And since we don't need to pass any data to this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 231.18,
          "end": 235.6,
          "en": "we can just set it as a value on the onClick prop like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 237.03,
          "end": 240.36,
          "en": "so that on this delete button, we're in the end calling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 240.36,
          "end": 243.303,
          "en": "the function received on that onDelete prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 244.38,
          "end": 248.13,
          "en": "And with that, if I save that, and I open my dev tools here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 248.13,
          "end": 252.36,
          "en": "to check if I'm getting any errors, if I click delete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 252.36,
          "end": 255.693,
          "en": "indeed the project is gone and I'm back to this screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 257.1,
          "end": 260.7,
          "en": "And if I quickly add two new projects just to check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 260.7,
          "end": 263.253,
          "en": "if the right project is being deleted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 266.79,
          "end": 271.02,
          "en": "like this and I now select the first one and click delete,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 271.02,
          "end": 273.153,
          "en": "you see that the other one is still there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 274.40999999999997,
          "end": 276.96,
          "en": "So that all seems to work and therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 276.96,
          "end": 280.29,
          "en": "now we can add projects, we can select projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 280.29,
          "end": 282.513,
          "en": "and we can also delete projects.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}